{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Issue 705: Explosive Runes makes Weapon Engraving: Fire detonate after 2 sec with 10% more critical damage",
  "contract": [
    "Explosive Runes 521219 (passive) reads 'Your Weapon Engraving: Fire now detonates after 2 sec and its critical",
    "damage is increased by $s2% (10%).' All three effects are native spell modifiers on family 38 mask1 0x10, which",
    "Weapon Engraving: Fire 653210 (Firebrand) carries: effect 0 flat SPELLMOD_DURATION -1000, effect 1 percent",
    "SPELLMOD_CRIT_DAMAGE_BONUS +10, effect 2 flat SPELLMOD_ACTIVATION_TIME -1000. Firebrand lasts 3000 ms",
    "(DurationIndex 27) and its periodic effects tick every 3000 ms, so it detonates when it expires. Expected with",
    "the talent: 2000 ms duration and amplitude and detonation at 2 sec while an untalented Runemaster's Firebrand",
    "still lasts 3 sec, and Firebrand's critical damage from a base of 1000 rises from 1500 to 1000 + 500 * 1.10 =",
    "1550. Unresolved: Firebrand's damage is its periodic tick, which this core lets crit only with aura 286, so the",
    "critical clause has no observable combat effect; it is not asserted beyond the native calculation. Firebrand is",
    "cast directly as a fixture instead of rolling Fire Engraving's 30% proc."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 90000,
